// The remote Vs' attitude groups (scripts/tandem/Attitudes.reds). Copies of
// the player's own group record (its default attitude and attitude to
// itself), under names of their own: an NPC made hostile to a group (vanilla
// AttitudeAgent.SetAttitudeTowardsAgentGroup) is hostile to every member, so
// in `player` hostility to one V reached every V (engine-knowledge §13.11).
// One group per puppet at a time (3 guests at most: endpoint.hpp kMaxGuests),
// and the shared one the puppet records start in.
//
// A group's relations to the others are not part of its record: they are
// Attitude records naming two groups (group1, group2, value). Ours are not
// listed here: scripts/tandem/AttitudeTweak.reds, a scripted tweak TweakXL
// runs as it loads this file, clones every Attitude record that names
// Attitudes.Group_Player once per group below, with the group in the
// player's place (Attitudes.TandemRelation<N>_<other group's name>, N the
// group's place below, from 0), so the list is the running game's own.
// Whether the engine's relation table takes them is logged at each start
// ("attitudes: declared relations ..."); the script still copies at run
// time what the records do not give.

Attitudes.Group_TandemPlayer : Attitudes.Group_Player {
  name = "tandem_player";
}

Attitudes.Group_TandemPlayer1 : Attitudes.Group_Player {
  name = "tandem_player_1";
}

Attitudes.Group_TandemPlayer2 : Attitudes.Group_Player {
  name = "tandem_player_2";
}

Attitudes.Group_TandemPlayer3 : Attitudes.Group_Player {
  name = "tandem_player_3";
}
